<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>ASHG abstracts: who and what gets a talk</title>
<style>
.viz-root {
  color-scheme: light;
  --surface-1: #fcfcfb; --surface-2: #f0efec; --rule: #e4e3df;
  --text-primary: #0b0b0b; --text-secondary: #52514e;
  --talk: #2a78d6; --poster: #e34948;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root:where(:not([data-theme="light"])) .viz-root {
    color-scheme: dark;
    --surface-1: #1a1a19; --surface-2: #383835; --rule: #383835;
    --text-primary: #f0efec; --text-secondary: #c3c2b7;
    --talk: #3987e5; --poster: #e66767;
  }
}
body { margin: 0; }
.viz-root { background: var(--surface-1); color: var(--text-primary); min-height: 100vh;
  font: 15px/1.5 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif; }
main { max-width: 980px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 32px 20px 64px; }
h1 { font-size: 28px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
h2 { font-size: 21px; margin: 40px 0 8px; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
h3 { font-size: 16px; margin: 24px 0 6px; }
p, li { color: var(--text-secondary); }
.caveat { background: var(--surface-2); border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; }
nav a { margin-right: 14px; color: var(--text-primary); }
img.figure { width: 100%; max-width: 760px; border-radius: 6px; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-size: 14px; }
th, td { padding: 5px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); text-align: right; }
td:not(.text) { white-space: nowrap; }
th:first-child, td:first-child, th.text, td.text { text-align: left; }
th { cursor: pointer; user-select: none; color: var(--text-secondary); font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
th[aria-sort="ascending"]::after { content: " ▲"; }
th[aria-sort="descending"]::after { content: " ▼"; }
.key { display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; margin-right: 6px; }
.scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
.cols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 24px; }
@media (max-width: 760px) { .cols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
footer { margin-top: 48px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-secondary); }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="viz-root"><main>
<h1>ASHG abstracts: who and what gets a talk</h1>
<p>Parsed from the ASHG annual meeting abstract booklets. Talks = platform + plenary presentations.</p>
<p class="caveat"><strong>Read this first.</strong> The booklets list only <em>accepted</em> abstracts, and authors
can ask for a poster. "Talk share" is the share of accepted abstracts presented as a talk, not an acceptance
rate or a quality score. All numbers are associations.</p>
<nav>{% for y in years %}<a href="#y{{ y.year }}">{{ y.year }}</a>{% endfor %}<a href="#methods">Methods</a></nav>

{% for y in years %}
<h2 id="y{{ y.year }}">ASHG {{ y.year }}</h2>
<p>{{ "{:,}".format(y.summary.abstracts) }} abstracts, {{ "{:,}".format(y.summary.talks) }} of them talks.
Baseline talk share <strong>{{ "%.1f"|format(100 * y.summary.talk_share) }}%</strong>.
{% if y.summary.truncated %}{{ y.summary.truncated }} abstracts ({{ y.summary.truncated_talks }} talks) are cut off
mid-text in the booklet itself. They count toward totals, the baseline and first-author credit, but not toward
senior-author credit (the author list is cut off) or the text analyses.{% endif %}</p>

<h3>Phrases that predict a talk</h3>
<p>The small panel at the bottom compares the largest sample size stated in each abstract
(e.g. "12,000 individuals", "N = 500 patients").</p>
<img class="figure" src="img/{{ y.year }}_headline.png" alt="Dot plot of the phrases most over-represented in ASHG {{ y.year }} talks versus posters, with odds ratios and 95% confidence intervals.">
<div class="cols">
{% for dir, label in [("talk", "More common in talks"), ("poster", "More common in posters")] %}
<div class="scroll"><p><span class="key" style="background: var(--{{ dir }})"></span><strong>{{ label }}</strong></p>
{{ y.premium[dir] }}</div>
{% endfor %}
</div>

<h3>Institutions</h3>
<img class="figure" src="img/{{ y.year }}_institutions.png" alt="Talk share with 95% intervals for the 20 institutions with the most ASHG {{ y.year }} abstracts by senior author.">
<p>Full top 50 by volume:</p>
<p>Credit goes to every institution of the senior (last) author; a second table credits the first author.
An abstract can count for several institutions, so the rows don't sum to the total.
First- and senior-author institutions agree for most abstracts.</p>
<div class="cols">
<div class="scroll"><p><strong>By senior author</strong></p>{{ y.institutions.senior }}</div>
<div class="scroll"><p><strong>By first author</strong></p>{{ y.institutions.first }}</div>
</div>

<h3>Senior authors with the highest talk share</h3>
<p>Among senior authors with at least {{ y.min_abstracts }} abstracts this year, ranked by the lower end of the
95% Wilson interval, so a 5-of-6 record outranks 2-of-2.</p>
<img class="figure" src="img/{{ y.year }}_senior_authors.png" alt="Talk share with 95% intervals for the top 10 senior authors at ASHG {{ y.year }}.">
<div class="scroll">{{ y.senior_authors }}</div>
{% endfor %}

<h2 id="methods">Methods</h2>
<ul>
<li>Text extracted with PyMuPDF and split into abstracts using each booklet's layout (titles, "Authors:", "Abstract:"). Every parsed abstract is checked against the booklet's table of contents, and a hand-checked sample of 55 abstracts is used as a test set.</li>
<li>Institutions: a hand-curated list of ~150 institutions and their spelling variants. Schools fold into their university (except Harvard Medical School); NIH institutes fold into NIH; hospitals and independent institutes stay separate.</li>
<li>Senior author = last listed person (consortium names skipped). The same person = same first + last name, and for common surnames also a shared institution.</li>
<li>Phrases: 1–3-word n-grams; per phrase, a talk-vs-poster odds ratio with +0.5 smoothing and a 95% CI, ranked by z-score. A phrase is dropped from the lists when a longer phrase containing it covers ≥90% of the same abstracts.</li>
</ul>
<footer>Code: <a href="{{ repo_url }}">{{ repo_url }}</a>. Booklets © ASHG; only aggregate results are published here.</footer>
</main></div>
<script>
document.querySelectorAll("table.sortable").forEach(table => {
  table.querySelectorAll("th").forEach((th, col) => th.addEventListener("click", () => {
    const asc = th.getAttribute("aria-sort") !== "ascending";
    table.querySelectorAll("th").forEach(h => h.removeAttribute("aria-sort"));
    th.setAttribute("aria-sort", asc ? "ascending" : "descending");
    const body = table.tBodies[0];
    const key = r => { const t = r.cells[col].dataset.v ?? r.cells[col].textContent; const n = parseFloat(t); return isNaN(n) ? t : n; };
    [...body.rows].sort((a, b) => { const x = key(a), y = key(b); return (x > y ? 1 : x < y ? -1 : 0) * (asc ? 1 : -1); })
      .forEach(r => body.appendChild(r));
  }));
});
</script>
</body>
</html>
